  "summary": "A bold impasto technique using a palette knife instead of brushes to apply thick, textured oil paint, associated with the Courtauld Institute's teaching methods.",
  "description": "This technique emphasizes the physicality of paint application, creating sculptural surfaces with visible knife marks and thick, expressive strokes. Developed and taught at the Courtauld Institute under figures like William Coldstream, it represented a reaction against more delicate brushwork and embraced the materiality of oil paint.",
